      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cross Bay Boulevard, which opened to traffic in 1925, earned its name because houses there sit 30 feet below the surrounding ground level.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ozone_Park",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "French immigrants Charles Lalance and Florian Grosjean founded a porcelain factory in the 1870s, built homes, and left only a clock tower after it closed in the 1960s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
